# Diff TypeScript as text even when a blob on one side contains a byte git reads
# as binary. `verify/registry.ts` carried a literal NUL as its map-key delimiter,
# which made git, GitHub and ripgrep classify the file as binary: GitHub rendered
# every change to it as "binary file not shown", and text searches skipped it in
# silence. The byte is now written as the escape `\x00`, but a diff is binary if
# EITHER side is, so without this the file stays unreviewable in any PR whose
# base still holds the old blob.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
*.mts diff
*.cts diff
